  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Empowering Fishing Communities in Uganda to Fight HIV and itsd I(mpact</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project centres on the islands of Kalangala District on Lake Victoria, Uganda, where HIV prevalence is 34%, compared to the national rate of 6.1%. General health and HIV support services are very limited and the islands can only be reached by powered canoes. Fishing is the main income source, done by men, which makes most women financially dependent on them. Although there is some knowledge of HIV, many people engage in multiple relationships and unprotected sex. Stigma and discrimination against people living with HIV is high and as a result many people are unwilling to be tested or disclose their HIV status. The project will increase knowledge and understanding of HIV and AIDS, fight stigma and discrimination, and help people to get voluntary counselling and testing, antiretroviral therapy, and home-based care.  Women will improve their incomes through small businesses.</narrative>
  </description>
